@ECHO OFF
REM The code page tests (make test-codepage-ega and so on): CONFIG.SYS is
REM each test's tests/codepage/NAME/config.sys, which loads DISPLAY.SYS, or
REM not. CPINFO prints the code page CON reports and the font in the
REM display's memory. MODE prepares and selects code pages from EGA.CPI,
REM KEYB follows CON's, CHCP (with NLSFUNC) switches DOS and CON together,
REM and then the errors.
CTTY AUX
ECHO GRDOS-TEST-BEGIN
ECHO == BOOT
CPINFO
MODE CON CP /STATUS
ECHO == PREPARE
MODE CON CP PREPARE=((850,865) A:\EGA.CPI)
MODE CON CP /STATUS
ECHO == SELECT
MODE CON CP SELECT=850
CPINFO
ECHO == KEYB
KEYB GR
KEYB
ECHO == CHCP
NLSFUNC A:\COUNTRY.SYS
CHCP
CHCP 437
CPINFO
KEYB
CHCP 850
CPINFO
ECHO == MODE
MODE CO80
CPINFO
ECHO == ERRORS
MODE CON CP SELECT=865
CHCP 865
MODE CON CP SELECT=860
MODE CON CP PREPARE=((860) A:\LCD.CPI)
MODE CON CP PREPARE=((999) A:\EGA.CPI)
MODE CON CP PREPARE=((850) A:\NOFILE.CPI)
MODE CON CP REFRESH
CPINFO
ECHO GRDOS-TEST-END
CTTY CON
